      "content": "wow that's a pretty intense perspective. i'll have to be careful how i phrase that in the memo. \n\ncould u explain a bit more about why you called the buyback strategy \"corporate greed\" and \"stock price manipulation\"? it seems like most finance textbooks teach that returning capital to shareholders is a standard, legitimate way to manage excess cash and reward owners. why is that viewed negatively in your view?",
